<title>SINGAPORE: Provisions Suppliers 96 net down 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Provisions Suppliers 96 net down 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				6.90 vs   7.07</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    3.00 vs   5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     3.55 vs   3.86</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)   3.07 vs   3.42</p>
<p>    Turnover				154.64 vs 146.66</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 3.61 vs   3.51</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    1.79 vs   1.31</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		2.87 vs   2.48</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  3.28 vs   4.05</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     7.58 vs   6.42</p>
<p>    Tax					 4.11 vs   3.72</p>
<p>    Minorities (expense)		  0.15 vs   0.33</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (loss)		1.01 vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    June 6, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  May 19, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Provisions Suppliers Corp Ltd is largely involved in consumer and industrial products with interests in the leisure and healthcare industries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
